[gd_scene load_steps=142 format=3]

; CORAL COVE — composed vertical slice for REQ-011.
;
; GAMEPLAY AUTHORITY IS STILL THE GREYBOX. Every mandatory platform, checkpoint,
; water volume, gate, hazard and collectible below keeps the measured route that
; the CoralRoute probe flies. This pass changes presentation, not the controller
; contract: the route remains run -> swim/dive/boost -> climb -> precision jumps
; -> gorge swim -> restoration -> finish.
;
; The earlier dressing pass proved the asset pipeline but scattered scenery
; uniformly across a 140 m corridor. Uniform density makes every metre equally
; important, which is the opposite of platformer composition. Dressing is now
; clustered around six authored beats: the opening frame, cove plunge, coral
; wall reveal, glow grotto compression, gorge release, and seed-bed payoff.
;
; Camera hints are declarative CameraHintVolume nodes from the shared client.
; They alter only framing, never input or physics. Visual motion is likewise a
; shared PresentationMotion helper attached only to meshes / decoration, so the
; collision proxy remains the one source of truth for traversal.

